  "notes": [
   "The set builds four separate pieces plus the figure: umbrella table with stool, oven, sink and cake. The cake is placed on top of the oven in the final step, so those two are linked in one graph.",
   "Element IDs with no catalogue entry were added as new types: 300101, 4650644, 415001, 4616174, 4183544, 4619596, 4220632, 4537936, 4618647, 4216479, 4618629, 4596240, 4600345, 4622859 and 4621993. Their ports are simplified guesses.",
   "The inventory lists 4x 614126, but only one is clearly shown, as the dark round plate on the oven top (page 8 step 3). The other three are not placed in any step, so they are omitted.",
   "Pink round plates 4517996 only have anti-stud.1 in the catalogue. Plates stacked on them use null ports on the lower side.",
   "The oven door 4219773 is shown hinged to the container front. The sandwich tray (tan plate with two pink plates and a brown plate) rests on the open door, so that link is a contact edge.",
   "The pole 4538720 is a rod with no studs. It is modelled as pushed into the centre stud of the 6x6 plate, with the umbrella top pushed onto its other end.",
   "Page 2 shows the figure assembly. The hair sits on the head, the head on the torso, and the torso on the legs and skirt, each joint turning freely.",
   "Page 11 shows the sink bricks. The two aqua panels sit between the white 1x2 bricks on the 2x4. Their exact stud positions are inferred, so each is joined to the 2x4 via its generic stud.1."
  ]
 },
